# APEX-OS — let a desktop user open a login screen on a spare VT.
#
# Fast user switching (P2-016 criterion 1). The switch to an account that is
# already logged in is `loginctl activate` and needs nothing: polkit's
# org.freedesktop.login1.chvt is allow_active=yes, read off this machine's own
# policy file. The switch to an account that is NOT logged in needs a second
# greetd instance on a spare VT, and starting a system unit from an
# unprivileged session is a polkit prompt — on a login path, from a compositor,
# with nobody able to answer it for a standard account.
#
# ALL, not %wheel. A standard account being able to switch users IS the
# criterion; restricting this to wheel would mean only administrators can share
# the machine, which is the opposite of what P2-016 asks for.
#
# The empty string after the command means "with no arguments at all". Without
# it sudoers grants the command with ANY arguments. Here that is not a
# tightening of a wide grant but the shape of the helper: it takes no arguments
# because an argument is a thing the caller chooses, and this helper chooses
# the VT, the config and the unit itself.
#
# What the grant is worth to a caller who is not meant to have it: nothing.
# The helper refuses unless SUDO_UID owns the ACTIVE session on seat0 — only
# the person at the keyboard can make the screen change — and refuses outright
# on a kiosk or auto-login machine. See its header.
ALL ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/apex-switch-greeter ""
